      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm going to add my two cents. Typically, I'm already in a VRChat world and then, using the Steam overlay, go to the Discord window and join a Voice Chat, either a room or a direct call to a friend.\n\nI'll hear a sound from VRChat, a low note, then see the \"You have lost connection\" or whatever message. I click OK, and then it rejoins the world.\n\nThis most recently happened while I was playing The Fate of the Irrbloss.\n\nThis has happened consistently across versions of Discord and VRChat.\n\nI suspect something about opening a UDP port for Discord VC somehow 'steals' the port from VRChat.\n\nI'm running Windows 11.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
